# Netlify _redirects — Tools site (tools.longboardtechnology.com)
#
# Proxy /api/* to the Render-hosted Flask backend (lt-tools).
# Status 200 = proxy (transparent), not 301/302 = redirect: the browser sees
# the response as if it came from tools.longboardtechnology.com, so requests
# are same-origin and no CORS plumbing is needed on the Flask side.
#
# Render still owns the API surface; only the static page assets moved here.

/api/*      https://lt-tools.onrender.com/api/:splat       200

# Glossary app — proxied from the same Render service via DispatcherMiddleware.
# /glossary  and  /glossary/anything  both route here.
/glossary*  https://lt-tools.onrender.com/glossary:splat  200
